#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/id #uuid "021d25c6-08db-5f20-a89b-110389d08e29" :question/math-academy-id "e-3224" :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/e0a6f6470cf511081c0dedf72450110f.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-1,1)$ and the radius of the circle is $r = 3$. Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - (-1))^{2} + (y - 1)^{2} &= 3^{2} \\\\\n(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 1)^{2} &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "e2d2147e-98df-54df-a271-4c5dff362a96" :question/math-academy-id "e-3226" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^2 + (y+4)^2 = 9$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y - (-4))^{2} &= 3^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a = 2$, $b =-4$, and $r = 3$.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-4)$ and its radius is $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087400 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "7e01a50d-62f1-5cc2-875e-bb085ef571c4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3230" :question/problem "The line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(3,4)$ and $(-1,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/ceca3bcfb8d6dd7f7f3fdba448fe0f44.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(3,4)$ and $Y(-1,2)$, we find that the length the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nXY &= \\sqrt{(-1 - 3)^{2} + (2 - 4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{20} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{XY}{2} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2}, \\dfrac {y_1+y_2}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\dfrac{3+(-1)}{2}, \\dfrac {4+2}{2}\\right)=(1,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nand center\n\n$$\n(a,b)=(1,3)\n$$\n\nand therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} &= (\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/id #uuid "16faff9a-9599-5b8c-85cd-132f3e3f4b92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6150" :question/problem "The circle above is centered at $C(2, 0)$ and the point $X(-1, 4)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/d44b59e332071b7cc4d32a6ddee9b2fb.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCX &= \\sqrt{(2 - (-1))^{2} + (0 - 4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y - 0)^{2} &= 5^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + y^{2} &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afce1979-fb12-5887-a4b8-07b4dc9efcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085838} {:answer/id #uuid "01864f4d-b973-5aa1-92f1-cb3921a89264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085839} {:answer/id #uuid "0f329018-4302-52b9-8a86-bbc96726874a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085840} {:answer/id #uuid "40dbe6a4-e1f9-5dda-af5e-c5d9cfb13938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 4)^{2} + (y - 4)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085841} {:answer/id #uuid "6fef7de2-a438-5793-89d4-f6ec87d20b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 4)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afce1979-fb12-5887-a4b8-07b4dc9efcc2" :answer/type {:db/id